# field-cad-text-align = Horizontal Alignment
# field-cad-text-anchor = Anchor Point Sketch
# field-cad-text-anchor-help = Aligns to a standalone sketch point. Constraints can move the point.
# field-cad-text-angle = Rotation
# field-cad-text-angle-help = Blank means 0. Example: 30 deg.
# field-cad-text-basis = Height Reference
# field-cad-text-basis-help = Character box uses full-width character size for Japanese engraving. Single-line fonts always use capital height.
# field-cad-text-chain = Follow Connected Curves
# field-cad-text-chain-help = Follows lines and arcs connected to the selected path, including polylines and rounded corners. Stops where three or more curves meet.
# field-cad-text-fit = Alignment Method
# field-cad-text-fit-width = Fit to Width
# field-cad-text-fit-width-help = Fits the longest text line to this width. Blank disables fitting.
# field-cad-text-font = Single-line Font
# field-cad-text-height = Text Height
# field-cad-text-outline-family = Outline Font
# field-cad-text-path = Path Sketch
# field-cad-text-path-help = Places text along a line, arc or circle. Position X is distance along the path; Y is distance from it.
# field-cad-text-reverse = Reverse Path
# field-cad-text-reverse-help = Circles and arcs run counterclockwise with text tops facing the center. Reversing faces the text outward, upright at the top of a circle.
# field-cad-text-spacing = Character Spacing
# field-cad-text-spacing-help = Additional spacing between characters. Blank means 0.
# field-cad-text-stroke = Stroke Width
# field-cad-text-stroke-help = Stroke thickness for recessed or raised extruded text. Blank uses 12% of capital height.
# field-cad-text-text = Text
# field-cad-text-valign = Vertical Alignment
# field-cad-text-width = Width Scale
# field-cad-text-width-help = Blank means 1.
# field-cad-text-x = Position X
# field-cad-text-x-help = Offset from the anchor point, if present.
# field-cad-text-y = Position Y
# field-cam-adaptive2d-air = Air Cuts in Cleared Areas
# field-cam-adaptive2d-air-help = Uses material removed by previous operations and setups, including before stock flips, to replace air cuts with rapid retract moves or short stay-down feeds. Uncertain areas remain. Re-evaluates this optimization in the actual order when exporting selected operations or grouping by tool.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-bottom-from = Bottom Height Reference
# field-cam-adaptive2d-bottom-from-help = Machining floor. Automatic uses the selected face, profile, hole bottom or similar reference.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-bottom-offset = Bottom Height Offset
# field-cam-adaptive2d-bottom-offset-help = A positive value stops above the floor, including Automatic. Example: 0.2 mm.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-depth = Depth from Sketch
# field-cam-adaptive2d-depth-help = Depth from the sketch plane to the floor, for example 3 mm. Blank places the floor on the sketch plane.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-entry = Entry Position
# field-cam-adaptive2d-entry-help = Use Place Entry in the 3D view. Starts at the nearest point that fits a helix. When blank, enters open faces from outside the stock and closed faces at their widest area.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-entry-kind = Entry Method
# field-cam-adaptive2d-entry-kind-help = Motion into the material. Helix descends around the entry position. Ramp descends along a loop. Plunge descends vertically and requires a center-cutting tool. Predrilled Hole descends into an existing hole; place the entry position at its center. Outside Stock descends outside the material and enters from the side.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-face = Floor Face
# field-cam-adaptive2d-faces = Additional Floor Faces
# field-cam-adaptive2d-faces-help = Select faces with Shift/Ctrl-click in the 3D view, then use Add Selected Faces or Remove Selected Faces.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-feed = Cutting Feed (mm/min)
# field-cam-adaptive2d-feed-from = Feed Height Reference
# field-cam-adaptive2d-feed-from-help = Height where rapid descent changes to cutting feed. Cannot be below Top Height.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-feed-help = Blank uses the tool default.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-feed-offset = Feed Height Offset
# field-cam-adaptive2d-feed-offset-help = Added to the reference height; negative lowers it. Example: 2 mm.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-fit = Arc Fitting Tolerance
# field-cam-adaptive2d-fit-help = Fits small line segments to arcs and longer lines within this tolerance, for example 0.005 mm. Reduces G-code size and smooths motion. Blank disables fitting.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-helix-diameter = Helix Diameter
# field-cam-adaptive2d-helix-diameter-help = Diameter traced by the tool center, for example 3 mm. Blank uses half the tool diameter. Shrinks to fit, falling back to a vertical plunge if necessary.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-last-step = Finishing Stepdown
# field-cam-adaptive2d-last-step-help = Uses a thinner final level for a clean floor, for example 0.2 mm. Blank divides all levels evenly.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-leave = Radial Stock to Leave
# field-cam-adaptive2d-leave-floor = Axial Stock to Leave
# field-cam-adaptive2d-leave-floor-help = Axial stock to leave. Blank uses the wall value. For example, rough walls with 0.3 mm stock and finish the floor with 0 mm.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-leave-help = Radial stock to leave. If the floor field is blank, leaves the same thickness on the floor.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-lift = Lift Height
# field-cam-adaptive2d-lift-help = Clearance above the machined floor or part during stay-down moves. Blank means 0.2 mm; 0 mm stays at floor height.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-load = Optimal Load
# field-cam-adaptive2d-load-help = Tool engagement width, for example 0.5 mm. Blank uses 15% of tool diameter. A smaller width allows deeper stepdown.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-min-radius = Minimum Cutting Radius
# field-cam-adaptive2d-min-radius-help = Rounds internal toolpath corners to at least this radius, for example 1 mm, to reduce tool engagement at corners. Leaves material in corners for wall finishing or rest machining. Blank disables rounding.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-plunge = Plunge Feed (mm/min)
# field-cam-adaptive2d-plunge-help = Blank uses the tool default.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-profile = Sketch Profile
# field-cam-adaptive2d-profile-help = Also machines inside closed profiles. If depth is blank, machines to the sketch plane.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-ramp-angle = Ramp Angle
# field-cam-adaptive2d-ramp-angle-help = For example 2 deg. Blank means 2 deg.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-ramp-feed = Ramp Feed (mm/min)
# field-cam-adaptive2d-ramp-feed-help = Feed for helical and ramp entries. Blank uses the cutting feed.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rest-corner = Rest Machining: Previous Tool Corner Radius
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rest-corner-help = For example 0.5 mm. Blank means 0 for a flat tool.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rest-diameter = Rest Machining: Previous Tool Diameter
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rest-diameter-help = For example 6.35 mm. Enter this when the previous tool is not in the tool library. A previous tool number takes precedence.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rest-tool = Rest Machining: Previous Tool Number
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rest-tool-help = Larger tool used on this face earlier. The current tool machines only corners it could not reach.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-retract = Retract Mode
# field-cam-adaptive2d-retract-help = Minimum Retract rises above the highest material along the move by the clearance allowance, never below stock top + 1 mm. Reduces vertical travel across cleared areas.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rpm = Spindle Speed (rpm)
# field-cam-adaptive2d-rpm-help = Blank uses the tool default.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-safe-from = Clearance Height Reference
# field-cam-adaptive2d-safe-from-help = Height for horizontal rapid moves. Automatic uses the setup's clearance height.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-safe-offset = Clearance Height Offset
# field-cam-adaptive2d-safe-offset-help = Added to the reference height; negative lowers it. Example: 3 mm.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-setup = Setup
# field-cam-adaptive2d-sim-grid = Simulation Resolution
# field-cam-adaptive2d-sim-grid-help = Grid resolution for simulating this operation. Coarse and Fine use the corresponding Simulation settings. Automatic uses Coarse for adaptive, pocket, face and 3D roughing, and Fine for other operations. Does not change the toolpath.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-stay-down = Stay-down Distance
# field-cam-adaptive2d-stay-down-help = Maximum distance to travel through cleared areas at cutting feed without retracting. Blank means 15 mm; 0 mm always retracts.
# field-cam-adaptive2d-stepdown = Stepdown
# field-cam-adaptive2d-stepdown-help = Blank uses the tool default.
