# field-cam-laser-feed = Speed (mm/min)
# field-cam-laser-feed-help = Travel speed while burning. Blank uses the tool's cutting feed.
# field-cam-laser-focus = Focus Offset
# field-cam-laser-focus-help = Laser height relative to the material surface; positive is upward. 0 focuses on the surface. Raise it to defocus for a wider mark.
# field-cam-laser-interval = Line Spacing
# field-cam-laser-interval-help = Spacing between parallel fill lines. A value near the laser spot diameter, such as 0.1 mm, is a useful starting point.
# field-cam-laser-kerf = Kerf Width
# field-cam-laser-kerf-help = Width removed by the laser. Blank uses the tool diameter (laser spot size). A starting estimate is half the difference between test-cut outside and inside dimensions.
# field-cam-laser-kerf-side = Kerf Compensation
# field-cam-laser-kerf-side-help = Offsets closed paths by half the kerf width to match the drawn dimensions. Keep Part offsets outer boundaries outward and holes inward. Cut Hole discards the interior. Open paths are not offset.
# field-cam-laser-lead-in = Lead-in
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-help = Enters a closed path from the scrap side to keep thick start marks and pierce holes off the part. Starts near the middle of the longest edge.
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-length = Lead-in Length
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-length-help = Straight lead length or arc radius. Blank means 1 mm.
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-line = Lead-in Linear Length
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-line-help = Straight segment tangent to the start of the arc. Blank means 0.
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-sweep = Lead-in Sweep Angle
# field-cam-laser-lead-in-sweep-help = Arc angle, greater than 0 and at most 180 degrees. Blank means 90 degrees.
# field-cam-laser-lead-out = Lead-out
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-help = Exits toward the scrap side after finishing a closed path.
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-length = Lead-out Length
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-length-help = Straight lead length or arc radius. Blank means 0.5 mm.
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-line = Lead-out Linear Length
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-line-help = Straight segment tangent to the end of the arc. Blank means 0.
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-sweep = Lead-out Sweep Angle
# field-cam-laser-lead-out-sweep-help = Arc angle, greater than 0 and at most 180 degrees. Blank means 90 degrees.
# field-cam-laser-mode = Laser Mode
# field-cam-laser-mode-help = Line traces sketch curves. Fill hatches closed regions, leaving holes in text unburned. Fill and Line fills first, then traces the boundary.
# field-cam-laser-overcut = Cut Overlap
# field-cam-laser-overcut-help = Burns beyond the start of a closed path on the final pass to avoid an uncut seam. Blank means 0.
# field-cam-laser-overscan = Overscan
# field-cam-laser-overscan-help = Distance beyond each pass end at the same speed and zero power. Avoids dark edges during acceleration and deceleration. Blank calculates from machine acceleration and speed, or uses 2 mm if unknown.
# field-cam-laser-passes = Pass Count
# field-cam-laser-passes-help = Number of passes over the same area. Increase for deeper engraving or cutting thin material.
# field-cam-laser-pierce-clearance = Pierce Clearance
# field-cam-laser-pierce-clearance-help = Moves the pierce point farther into the scrap side before the lead-in. Adds to its initial straight segment. Even without a lead-in, enters along a straight segment of this length. Blank means 0.
# field-cam-laser-pierce-height = Pierce Height
# field-cam-laser-pierce-height-help = Pierces above the cutting height and descends while burning to widen the initial hole. Blank pierces at cutting height.
# field-cam-laser-pierce-time = Pierce Time (s)
# field-cam-laser-pierce-time-help = Burns in place at the start for this duration, useful for thick material. 0 disables dwell. Unavailable on machines that fire only while moving, such as Carvera Air.
# field-cam-laser-rpm = Power (%)
# field-cam-laser-rpm-help = 0–100. Blank uses the tool's cutting condition; laser tools use the spindle speed field for power.
